  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure centered over the Great Lakes will\ncontinue to build southeastward today, becoming centered over\nthe Mid-Atlantic and Carolinas Tuesday, before sliding offshore\nWed. This will keep a cooler/drier NE-E flow over the area, with\nseasonable temps for early September and feeling much more \ncomfortable, with highs in the 80s and dewpoints in the 60s/low \n70s. Temps will begin to warm mid to late week as southerly flow\nre-develops ahead of the next front. Isolated coastal showers \nwill be possible today, with bulk of activity remaining \noffshore. Mostly dry weather will then prevail through mid week\nwith drier air in place. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...The next front will approach the area late week,\npossibly stalling over the area into the weekend. This will lead\nto increasing precip chances Fri and Sat.",
